        rdfs:comment                   "Circular christening tablecloth. Hexagonal mesh net with overall appliqued small dots, center medallion and border of leaf fronds, scalloped edge. Net centered on white silk satin encircles by stitched-down pleated ruffle. Used by Prince Constantin Belosselsky-Belozersky in Russia, 1843.  (Cf. 48.1239-43)."@en ;
